       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 600 mg once daily is three times the FDA-labeled maximum of 200 mg/day. Nothing in the details you gave (normal renal and hepatic function, 70 kg, no allergies) would justify a dose that high. At that level the risks include serotonin syndrome, seizures, QT prolongation, and severe GI or bleeding effects.\n\nPlease clarify which of these applies:\n\n1. **It's a typo or unit error.** For example, you may have meant 50 mg or 100 mg, or 200 mg at most. Tell me the intended dose and I'll enter it right away.\n2. **It's intentional.** For example, you may be treating a refractory case under a specialist plan. If so, confirm that explicitly and tell me what to put in the order note, such as the rationale or monitoring plan. I'd also suggest checking with pharmacy, since they will likely flag it anyway.\n\nFor reference, typical adult dosing is 50 mg daily to start for depression, titrated in 25\u201350 mg steps to 50\u2013200 mg daily."
